1
00:00:05,534 --> 00:00:07,051
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,134 --> 00:00:09,184
(Filming complied with guidelines
for children, youth, and animals.)

3
00:00:09,534 --> 00:00:11,367
(2017)

4
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:13,701
(Episode 1)

5
00:00:20,767 --> 00:00:21,767
Hello.

6
00:00:25,201 --> 00:00:27,667
I took the wrong bus,
so I got off partway.

7
00:00:29,467 --> 00:00:31,267
I was lost in thought.

8
00:00:33,467 --> 00:00:34,634
What?

9
00:00:36,001 --> 00:00:38,001
Yeah, it's my first day. Why?

10
00:00:39,767 --> 00:00:42,367
Forget it, I'm hanging up.

11
00:00:55,661 --> 00:00:56,667
Why?

12
00:00:56,967 --> 00:00:58,001
Matching shirts.

13
00:00:58,201 --> 00:00:59,201
What?

14
00:01:00,801 --> 00:01:01,901
You two are a couple, right?

15
00:01:02,025 --> 00:01:03,110
What couple?

16
00:01:03,135 --> 00:01:04,567
Sure looks like it.

17
00:01:15,467 --> 00:01:17,367
Quick as lightning.

18
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:40,734
Ta-da!

19
00:01:41,034 --> 00:01:44,834
Amazing!

20
00:01:45,134 --> 00:01:47,201
You're seriously so cool!

21
00:01:47,534 --> 00:01:49,534
Can you teach me that trick?

22
00:01:50,067 --> 00:01:51,134
Me too!

23
00:01:51,134 --> 00:01:53,060
- Me too!
- The bus is here.

24
00:01:53,934 --> 00:01:54,934
See you next time.

25
00:02:17,967 --> 00:02:19,034
We match, don't we?

26
00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:21,401
Sorry?

27
00:02:21,534 --> 00:02:24,434
GB TV Shopping, six for 59.9 dollars.

28
00:02:29,334 --> 00:02:32,867
Amazing quality for the price.
They wash great, too!

29
00:02:34,934 --> 00:02:36,584
Do you work for the company?

30
00:02:36,667 --> 00:02:39,467
No, I'm just a customer.

31
00:02:40,001 --> 00:02:43,284
That green you're wearing suits you,

32
00:02:43,367 --> 00:02:45,251
but there's a purple in the set of six.

33
00:02:45,276 --> 00:02:46,876
That one's really pretty, too.

34
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:48,167
Sure.

35
00:02:53,767 --> 00:02:56,451
I saw you playing so well
with those kids earlier.

36
00:02:56,534 --> 00:02:59,801
They're my little siblings' age.

37
00:03:02,534 --> 00:03:03,534
Ma'am.

38
00:03:05,367 --> 00:03:06,601
Is she asleep?

39
00:03:07,967 --> 00:03:10,201
Ma'am, are you okay?

40
00:03:41,401 --> 00:03:44,501
Sir, please open the door.

41
00:03:47,834 --> 00:03:53,534
Ma'am, are you all right?

42
00:04:02,667 --> 00:04:04,101
Ma'am!

43
00:04:09,534 --> 00:04:15,184
Gyu Rim will be training you from now on.

44
00:04:15,267 --> 00:04:16,767
Han Gyu Rim!

45
00:04:19,001 --> 00:04:20,201
Where's Han Gyu Rim?

46
00:04:20,767 --> 00:04:23,767
She said she'd be a little late today.

47
00:04:24,167 --> 00:04:25,167
Why?

48
00:04:25,434 --> 00:04:30,567
Some elderly woman collapsed,
so she's taking her to the hospital.

49
00:04:33,301 --> 00:04:35,084
She picked the wrong job.

50
00:04:35,167 --> 00:04:37,867
She should go work for 911,
not wait tables at a restaurant.

51
00:04:38,934 --> 00:04:41,518
Her nickname used to be Inspector Han.

52
00:04:41,601 --> 00:04:47,401
Whenever someone's in trouble,
she's sure to appear. Inspector Han.

53
00:04:51,601 --> 00:04:55,867
Ma'am, are you okay?
Are you coming around?

54
00:04:57,767 --> 00:04:59,184
And who might you be?

55
00:04:59,267 --> 00:05:01,951
I was at the bus stop earlier.

56
00:05:02,034 --> 00:05:05,151
They said you fainted
because you're very weak.

57
00:05:05,234 --> 00:05:07,801
I called your son. He'll be here soon.

58
00:05:08,034 --> 00:05:13,001
Mom! Park Sun A!

59
00:05:14,001 --> 00:05:18,367
- Mom, are you okay?
- That hurts, you brat.

60
00:05:19,134 --> 00:05:23,001
If you felt off, you should've
seen a doctor first.

61
00:05:23,267 --> 00:05:26,518
If something had happened to you,
I'd have gone with you, I swear.

62
00:05:26,601 --> 00:05:28,118
I should get going now.

63
00:05:28,201 --> 00:05:32,918
You're the one who found my mom
and called me, right?

64
00:05:33,001 --> 00:05:34,834
- Yes.
- Wait!

65
00:05:35,101 --> 00:05:38,834
How could I let the person who saved
my mother's life just walk off?

66
00:05:39,301 --> 00:05:41,018
I'm no lifesaver.

67
00:05:41,101 --> 00:05:42,884
- It's fine.
- Take good care of your mother,

68
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:47,767
- Ma'am, get well soon! Take care!
- Hey! Young lady!

69
00:05:48,301 --> 00:05:49,401
Heung Sik!

70
00:05:50,134 --> 00:05:51,234
Mom!

71
00:05:52,767 --> 00:05:54,034
Mom, you okay?

72
00:05:54,667 --> 00:05:58,767
Is there another girl
as kind as her these days?

73
00:05:59,534 --> 00:06:02,484
Maybe, but they're nearly extinct.

74
00:06:02,567 --> 00:06:05,251
When I opened my eyes earlier,

75
00:06:05,334 --> 00:06:08,051
I thought I was seeing an angel.

76
00:06:08,134 --> 00:06:09,134
Did you?

77
00:06:11,501 --> 00:06:12,818
What's our family motto?

78
00:06:12,901 --> 00:06:15,967
Repay a grudge twofold,
repay a kindness a thousandfold.

79
00:06:16,601 --> 00:06:18,284
You must repay it.

80
00:06:18,367 --> 00:06:21,284
Ignoring a kindness
makes you no better than a beast.

81
00:06:21,367 --> 00:06:23,001
Got it, Mom. Don't worry.

82
00:06:23,467 --> 00:06:24,884
Just stop getting sick, please.

83
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:26,767
What's that girl's name?

84
00:06:27,501 --> 00:06:28,718
You'd know before me. How would I?

85
00:06:28,743 --> 00:06:30,643
You didn't even get her name?

86
00:06:30,834 --> 00:06:31,834
You don't know it, Mom?

87
00:06:31,967 --> 00:06:34,134
How would I? I just woke up.

88
00:06:34,434 --> 00:06:36,001
- What do we do?
- You idiot.

89
00:06:42,534 --> 00:06:43,534
Han Gyu Rim!

90
00:06:46,501 --> 00:06:47,501
Manager!

91
00:06:50,301 --> 00:06:51,567
What are you smiling about?

92
00:06:51,834 --> 00:06:54,467
A smile won't save you from me,
you know that.

93
00:06:55,201 --> 00:07:00,834
Didn't I say if volunteering's your dream,
just quit and go chase it?

94
00:07:01,901 --> 00:07:03,001
I'm sorry.

95
00:07:03,901 --> 00:07:08,867
I'll do the bar and floor closing
every day for a month, no rotation.

96
00:07:09,301 --> 00:07:13,501
So please give me one more chance.

97
00:07:14,834 --> 00:07:17,501
Well, if you're going that far.

98
00:07:18,101 --> 00:07:22,534
Then Gyu Rim will handle the floor
and bar closing for a month.

99
00:07:29,567 --> 00:07:32,867
This is Kim Mu Jin, starting today.

100
00:07:34,767 --> 00:07:36,634
Gyu Rim, you can train Mu Jin well, right?

101
00:07:36,733 --> 00:07:37,900
Yes, of course.

102
00:07:40,513 --> 00:07:41,997
We've met before, right?

103
00:07:42,201 --> 00:07:45,367
Yeah. 59.9 dollars.

104
00:07:47,934 --> 00:07:49,534
I look forward to working with you.

105
00:07:49,867 --> 00:07:51,267
Yeah, likewise.

106
00:07:53,934 --> 00:07:56,201
Mom, isn't my Gyu Yeong lovely?

107
00:07:56,534 --> 00:07:57,534
She is.

108
00:07:58,067 --> 00:08:00,967
Where did you find such a pretty,
well-mannered young lady?

109
00:08:01,934 --> 00:08:04,267
She's just like your mom
when she was young.

110
00:08:04,401 --> 00:08:07,101
Honey! She's far prettier than me!

111
00:08:07,867 --> 00:08:09,967
You're more beautiful.

112
00:08:10,867 --> 00:08:13,634
I thought you were just a pretty face,
but you're sweet-spoken, too.

113
00:08:14,534 --> 00:08:16,967
You're in med school?

114
00:08:17,467 --> 00:08:18,651
Yes, that's right.

115
00:08:18,734 --> 00:08:23,101
Dad, Gyu Yeong isn't just a pretty face.
She's smart, too.

116
00:08:24,367 --> 00:08:25,634
Hey, snap out of it, you fool.

117
00:08:34,434 --> 00:08:36,334
It's really you, Han Gyu Yeong.

118
00:08:40,434 --> 00:08:42,501
How many months is this one?

119
00:08:42,734 --> 00:08:44,034
Excuse me, ma'am.

120
00:08:44,167 --> 00:08:46,084
Wait, who are you?

121
00:08:46,167 --> 00:08:48,001
Who on earth do you think you are...

122
00:08:48,234 --> 00:08:52,184
Looks like you've fallen under the spell
of a thousand-year-old fox,

123
00:08:52,267 --> 00:08:54,551
so I couldn't just look away.

124
00:08:54,634 --> 00:08:56,367
Why are you being so cruel?

125
00:08:56,467 --> 00:08:59,467
This girl? She's a real terror.

126
00:09:00,001 --> 00:09:03,434
At first glance, you don't seem
to come from an ordinary family.

127
00:09:04,101 --> 00:09:06,434
Which is why she seduced him, I bet.

128
00:09:06,667 --> 00:09:07,734
Ma'am!

129
00:09:07,934 --> 00:09:09,034
Gyu Yeong!

130
00:09:09,867 --> 00:09:11,951
- Do you know this woman?
- Of course she does. She knows me!

131
00:09:12,034 --> 00:09:15,001
I know her all too well.

132
00:09:15,367 --> 00:09:19,451
Just because she's pretty
and attends a prestigious med school...

133
00:09:19,534 --> 00:09:22,184
she acts like she's already
a fully licensed doctor,

134
00:09:22,267 --> 00:09:25,934
using one man after another
for everything they're worth,

135
00:09:26,301 --> 00:09:30,634
then tossing them aside
once she's gotten what she wants.

136
00:09:45,834 --> 00:09:49,134
I have somewhere to be, so excuse me.

137
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:52,901
I'd love to treat you both
to a nice meal sometime soon.

138
00:09:58,267 --> 00:10:01,784
I heard her longest relationship
only lasted eight months.

139
00:10:01,867 --> 00:10:02,867
Is that right?

140
00:10:03,934 --> 00:10:06,601
Keep dreaming, ma'am.

141
00:10:10,034 --> 00:10:14,067
My son is still seeing a psychiatrist
because of her.

142
00:10:14,767 --> 00:10:17,701
- If you don't want your son wrecked...
- Ma'am!

143
00:10:23,101 --> 00:10:26,301
I think you should know the truth.

144
00:10:26,467 --> 00:10:29,084
I broke up with your son,

145
00:10:29,167 --> 00:10:33,784
because he kept sleeping with bar girls
while we were together.

146
00:10:33,867 --> 00:10:36,801
- So I dumped him because he disgusted me.
- What?

147
00:10:37,434 --> 00:10:42,218
Your son begged me to take him back,
saying it was all his fault...

148
00:10:42,301 --> 00:10:44,967
I couldn't stand him, so I exposed it all,

149
00:10:45,767 --> 00:10:47,467
and it turned out he'd even been charged
with attempted rape.

150
00:10:48,667 --> 00:10:52,234
He's seeing a psychiatrist
for a lighter sentence.

151
00:10:52,734 --> 00:10:55,184
Well, since you've
already blown this whole thing up,

152
00:10:55,267 --> 00:10:59,534
want me to tell you just how much
of a piece of trash your son really is?

153
00:11:01,801 --> 00:11:07,634
Gyu Yeong! Han Gyu Yeong!
You can't just leave like this!

154
00:11:08,701 --> 00:11:10,118
I'll take care of everything.

155
00:11:10,201 --> 00:11:12,467
If Mom and Dad turn against you
because of today...

156
00:11:15,834 --> 00:11:17,701
I can give them up, too.

157
00:11:18,201 --> 00:11:20,684
I only need you. So, Gyu Yeong, let's...

158
00:11:20,767 --> 00:11:22,401
Then why would I be with you?

159
00:11:23,133 --> 00:11:24,134
What?

160
00:11:24,134 --> 00:11:27,351
If you give up your parents'
money and connections,

161
00:11:27,434 --> 00:11:30,667
you're just a loser with no future.

162
00:11:30,801 --> 00:11:32,101
So why would I date you?

163
00:11:33,901 --> 00:11:37,567
You said you loved me.

164
00:11:39,001 --> 00:11:41,767
You said you were crazy about me!

165
00:11:45,534 --> 00:11:47,418
I am.

166
00:11:47,501 --> 00:11:52,118
I love your money, your nice car,
your designer clothes,

167
00:11:52,201 --> 00:11:54,834
and the future that's
already laid out for you.

168
00:11:55,334 --> 00:11:57,367
That's what I'm crazy about.

169
00:11:57,607 --> 00:11:58,607
Gyu Yeong.

170
00:11:59,934 --> 00:12:02,701
If you want me back,
convince your parents.

171
00:12:02,834 --> 00:12:04,934
Tell them it's Han Gyu Yeong or death.

172
00:12:05,601 --> 00:12:07,834
Surely they won't kill their only son,
right?

173
00:12:12,801 --> 00:12:15,301
Gyu Yeong!

174
00:12:17,167 --> 00:12:19,367
- Hey, Han Gyu O. Where are you going?
- Cram school.

175
00:12:19,401 --> 00:12:21,301
Heard you're prepping for sports
college. Going well?

176
00:12:22,134 --> 00:12:23,134
Just doing what I can.

177
00:12:23,301 --> 00:12:24,301
Hey, hang in there.

178
00:12:24,434 --> 00:12:26,934
- Yeah, I'm free till 11.
- Till 11?

179
00:12:28,434 --> 00:12:29,634
Hey, did you bring your coins?

180
00:12:30,267 --> 00:12:32,331
- I don't have any.
- Sure you don't.

181
00:12:32,701 --> 00:12:34,168
This punk. He's faking.

182
00:12:34,202 --> 00:12:35,451
Hey, Gyu O.

183
00:12:35,534 --> 00:12:36,534
Let's just go.

184
00:12:36,734 --> 00:12:38,901
I hear jingling in your bag, though.

185
00:12:39,103 --> 00:12:40,169
Come on, Gyu O.

186
00:12:41,401 --> 00:12:42,434
Go on ahead.

187
00:12:44,901 --> 00:12:45,967
We'll head off, then.

188
00:12:53,367 --> 00:12:56,001
Yeong Jun. Let's do this the easy way.

189
00:12:59,401 --> 00:13:00,901
This punk's ignoring me again.

190
00:13:01,134 --> 00:13:03,584
Hey, when I talk, you listen.

191
00:13:03,667 --> 00:13:06,801
Why do you keep making this hard?

192
00:13:14,467 --> 00:13:15,467
What's this?

193
00:13:19,567 --> 00:13:20,567
Gyu O.

194
00:13:22,034 --> 00:13:23,034
Get up.

195
00:13:23,834 --> 00:13:24,834
Yeah.

196
00:13:27,001 --> 00:13:28,484
What are you doing?

197
00:13:28,567 --> 00:13:32,034
Quit showing off before you get
beat, and just walk away.

198
00:13:35,767 --> 00:13:36,767
I'd rather not.

199
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,160
You'd rather not?

200
00:13:40,201 --> 00:13:41,567
This brat!

201
00:13:43,267 --> 00:13:45,067
Hey. You okay?

202
00:13:49,772 --> 00:13:51,287
You little brat!

203
00:13:52,734 --> 00:13:55,734
Hit him more! Do it!

204
00:14:38,034 --> 00:14:42,067
Ribeye, garlic, pepperoni,
and what was the last one?

205
00:14:58,734 --> 00:15:00,218
Is there another problem?

206
00:15:00,243 --> 00:15:01,776
This is really going too far.

207
00:15:03,134 --> 00:15:04,567
Can't you understand me?

208
00:15:04,701 --> 00:15:08,567
I asked for medium rare, closer to rare.
What is this?

209
00:15:08,834 --> 00:15:11,367
First it was rare, now it's medium.

210
00:15:12,373 --> 00:15:13,806
Can't you cook it evenly?

211
00:15:14,067 --> 00:15:16,118
And the garnish, I asked for it well done,

212
00:15:16,201 --> 00:15:18,934
This isn't well done. It's medium well.

213
00:15:19,434 --> 00:15:23,734
And there was a hair in it, too.

214
00:15:25,567 --> 00:15:27,534
First of all, I apologize.

215
00:15:28,434 --> 00:15:33,184
But this hair is long and wavy,

216
00:15:33,267 --> 00:15:36,301
and none of our staff have hair like that.

217
00:15:36,376 --> 00:15:37,472
Excuse me?

218
00:15:37,535 --> 00:15:40,251
Are you saying we're just
making up complaints?

219
00:15:40,334 --> 00:15:41,901
Forget it. Let's go.

220
00:15:46,067 --> 00:15:50,401
I won't pay a single cent
for garbage food like this, got it?

221
00:15:52,201 --> 00:15:54,434
I'm going live the second I leave.

222
00:15:54,510 --> 00:15:57,410
They won't admit they were wrong
or even apologize.

223
00:15:57,582 --> 00:16:02,539
Don't waste your time or money
on a place that blames customers.

224
00:16:37,234 --> 00:16:38,834
My arm's going to fall off.

225
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:51,267
That upset you a lot, didn't it?

226
00:16:53,001 --> 00:16:56,267
You were angry and felt wronged, too.

227
00:16:56,631 --> 00:17:00,367
Why did this happen to me?
How do I get back at them?

228
00:17:00,901 --> 00:17:02,601
Should I even keep this job?

229
00:17:02,901 --> 00:17:04,901
Should I just quit already?

230
00:17:06,967 --> 00:17:08,334
When that happens,

231
00:17:22,109 --> 00:17:28,976
when you're angry, hurt, and wronged,
you drink sweet cocoa like this.

232
00:17:29,467 --> 00:17:32,134
And then you cast a spell.

233
00:17:33,367 --> 00:17:36,434
It's nothing. It's no big deal.

234
00:17:37,634 --> 00:17:40,034
Forget it all. Erase it.

235
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:45,634
Dwelling on it only hurts you.
Want to give it a try?

236
00:17:50,028 --> 00:17:51,061
Should I drink it?

237
00:17:57,901 --> 00:18:03,918
Then close your eyes, breathe deep,
and cast the spell inside.

238
00:18:04,001 --> 00:18:05,567
Close your eyes.

239
00:18:12,667 --> 00:18:15,867
It's nothing. It's no big deal.

240
00:18:16,401 --> 00:18:19,867
See if I give you an inch
of my heart or memory.

241
00:18:20,167 --> 00:18:21,767
Act up all you want.

242
00:18:21,901 --> 00:18:25,934
See if a single hair or lash
of mine even twitches.

243
00:18:26,352 --> 00:18:30,486
Now open your eyes,
and do it with a big smile.

244
00:18:31,101 --> 00:18:32,167
Do I really have to smile?

245
00:18:32,401 --> 00:18:33,801
Yes, you really do.

246
00:18:34,101 --> 00:18:35,467
That's how it truly lifts.

247
00:18:36,534 --> 00:18:37,701
I don't really feel like smiling.

248
00:18:37,934 --> 00:18:40,134
You came this far, why be stubborn?

249
00:18:40,434 --> 00:18:42,367
Just humor me and try it.

250
00:18:49,267 --> 00:18:52,167
Well done. Feels lighter, right?

251
00:18:55,452 --> 00:18:58,436
Angry, hurt, wronged...

252
00:18:58,549 --> 00:19:00,999
It'd be best if things like that
never happened,

253
00:19:01,167 --> 00:19:03,734
but even if you meet such things
and such people,

254
00:19:03,901 --> 00:19:06,134
don't let them eat you alive.

255
00:19:07,067 --> 00:19:10,034
Cheer up. And don't quit your job!

256
00:19:11,467 --> 00:19:12,601
That's reassuring.

257
00:19:12,834 --> 00:19:14,167
That's just how I am.

258
00:19:16,801 --> 00:19:20,184
And those awful customers planting
the hair in the steak,

259
00:19:20,267 --> 00:19:25,234
it got caught perfectly on camera.
Crystal clear, too.

260
00:19:25,967 --> 00:19:27,301
Really?

261
00:19:30,801 --> 00:19:33,667
These days, karma settles up a lot faster.

262
00:19:42,434 --> 00:19:44,118
Yes, hello?

263
00:19:44,201 --> 00:19:45,601
Yes, speaking?

264
00:19:46,834 --> 00:19:48,101
Sorry?

265
00:19:49,101 --> 00:19:51,201
Yes! I'll come right away.

266
00:19:52,801 --> 00:19:54,934
I have to run. I'm sorry.

267
00:20:01,401 --> 00:20:05,457
- Look!
- No, my handsome son's face!

268
00:20:05,482 --> 00:20:06,934
Stop overreacting!

269
00:20:07,834 --> 00:20:08,834
(Cho Yeong Jun)

270
00:20:11,767 --> 00:20:12,901
Hey, you little punk.

271
00:20:13,218 --> 00:20:16,434
How dare you touch my son
when even I treat him like glass?

272
00:20:16,563 --> 00:20:18,001
What do you think you're doing?

273
00:20:19,401 --> 00:20:20,701
Everyone, please sit down.

274
00:20:21,667 --> 00:20:24,734
Please, everyone, calm down.

275
00:20:25,334 --> 00:20:26,567
Calm down?

276
00:20:27,201 --> 00:20:28,618
Discipline committee teacher,

277
00:20:28,701 --> 00:20:30,367
You think we can calm down now?

278
00:20:30,734 --> 00:20:33,834
Our kids left for school fine and got
beaten to a pulp within hours.

279
00:20:34,201 --> 00:20:37,234
Don't even think of brushing
this hearing under the rug.

280
00:20:37,401 --> 00:20:40,542
I'll get this thug transferred
or expelled, at the very least.

281
00:20:40,567 --> 00:20:42,234
I won't let this slide, so...

282
00:20:44,001 --> 00:20:46,734
please investigate what happened
to Yeong Jun and punish them.

283
00:20:47,401 --> 00:20:51,751
They extorted him, stole his shoes
and clothes, bullied him, and beat him,

284
00:20:51,834 --> 00:20:54,534
and made him do all kinds of vile things.

285
00:20:54,667 --> 00:20:56,267
Listen to him!

286
00:20:56,393 --> 00:20:59,101
My boy is so gentle and sweet.

287
00:21:00,051 --> 00:21:03,434
He sneers while an adult is talking.

288
00:21:03,667 --> 00:21:06,467
What kind of upbringing did he have...

289
00:21:06,834 --> 00:21:08,901
Look at his eyes changing.

290
00:21:08,926 --> 00:21:11,392
Careful, he might hit us next.

291
00:21:11,767 --> 00:21:13,567
Hey, watch how you look at me.

292
00:21:13,934 --> 00:21:15,401
The nerve of this rude boy.

293
00:21:16,101 --> 00:21:17,551
I'm sorry.

294
00:21:17,634 --> 00:21:20,551
Please, let it go just this once.

295
00:21:20,634 --> 00:21:21,867
Come on!

296
00:21:22,101 --> 00:21:23,201
Apologize now.

297
00:21:23,301 --> 00:21:24,534
- Look how stiff his neck is.
- Gyu O!

298
00:21:24,559 --> 00:21:25,645
Aren't you going to apologize?

299
00:21:25,670 --> 00:21:26,670
- Seriously...
- Unbelievable.

300
00:21:27,534 --> 00:21:28,534
Hey!

301
00:21:28,967 --> 00:21:30,034
This little brat!

302
00:21:30,059 --> 00:21:31,111
Why, this kid!

303
00:21:31,136 --> 00:21:32,620
What do you think you're doing?

304
00:21:32,707 --> 00:21:33,707
What?

305
00:21:39,667 --> 00:21:40,667
Let me see.

306
00:21:42,201 --> 00:21:44,401
Let me see how hurt you are.

307
00:21:44,634 --> 00:21:47,201
Hey, lady, who are you?

308
00:21:48,434 --> 00:21:49,534
I'm Han Gyu O's sister.

309
00:21:49,834 --> 00:21:51,501
Not the sister, get the parents.

310
00:21:51,601 --> 00:21:54,201
What a terrible way to raise a kid.

311
00:21:54,367 --> 00:21:55,934
We don't have any parents.

312
00:21:56,234 --> 00:21:57,301
Talk to me.

313
00:21:58,801 --> 00:22:00,401
So he's got no parents.

314
00:22:00,834 --> 00:22:03,267
No wonder the brat turned out like that.

315
00:22:03,557 --> 00:22:05,976
Officers, what are you doing?

316
00:22:06,001 --> 00:22:08,618
Throw that thug behind bars,

317
00:22:08,701 --> 00:22:10,109
and let our boys go already.

318
00:22:10,134 --> 00:22:12,967
They've got cram school
and so much else to do.

319
00:22:13,134 --> 00:22:14,784
Aren't you being too harsh?

320
00:22:14,867 --> 00:22:16,601
Harsh? How is this harsh?

321
00:22:17,101 --> 00:22:20,401
You beat other people's sons
to a pulp and call me harsh?

322
00:22:20,601 --> 00:22:23,884
When you should be on your knees
begging for mercy,

323
00:22:23,967 --> 00:22:26,101
how dare you stare me down?

324
00:22:26,126 --> 00:22:28,051
I heard your sons started it.

325
00:22:28,120 --> 00:22:31,184
- What?
- They hit and bullied Yeong Jun first.

326
00:22:31,267 --> 00:22:32,684
Gyu O stepped in to stop them.

327
00:22:32,709 --> 00:22:34,118
This girl...

328
00:22:34,201 --> 00:22:36,218
Who bullied whom, exactly?

329
00:22:36,301 --> 00:22:37,967
Our boys just, you know.

330
00:22:38,167 --> 00:22:39,918
They thought Yeong Jun was cute.

331
00:22:40,001 --> 00:22:43,734
It was just harmless fun,
but that thug took it the wrong way.

332
00:22:50,885 --> 00:22:52,152
The wrong way?

333
00:22:52,734 --> 00:22:54,234
Fun?

334
00:22:55,242 --> 00:22:58,709
If that's fun,
then Gyu O was just having fun, too.

335
00:22:59,534 --> 00:23:01,218
He must've found them real cute.

336
00:23:01,301 --> 00:23:03,393
What is this crazy girl saying?

337
00:23:03,501 --> 00:23:04,584
Yeong Jun can tell us.

338
00:23:04,667 --> 00:23:07,034
Was it fun, or violence?

339
00:23:14,401 --> 00:23:15,501
Yeong Jun.

340
00:23:25,034 --> 00:23:26,467
Yeong Jun.

341
00:23:27,846 --> 00:23:29,646
It was just fun.

342
00:23:31,434 --> 00:23:34,701
But Gyu O misunderstood.

343
00:23:35,534 --> 00:23:38,184
Yeong Jun, that's not true.

344
00:23:38,267 --> 00:23:42,601
- They bullied you, so Gyu O...
- They weren't bullying me.

345
00:23:46,734 --> 00:23:49,301
Then how do you explain
getting hurt like this?

346
00:23:49,434 --> 00:23:52,234
Who calls this harmless fun?

347
00:23:54,534 --> 00:23:56,301
Gyu O did this.

348
00:23:58,201 --> 00:24:03,184
I got this trying to stop Gyu O,
and he hit me.

349
00:24:03,267 --> 00:24:04,467
What?

350
00:24:04,634 --> 00:24:08,267
Hey, Cho Yeong Jun. Tell the truth.

351
00:24:09,967 --> 00:24:11,351
Tell them the truth!

352
00:24:11,434 --> 00:24:12,995
Say it straight, you punk!

353
00:24:13,334 --> 00:24:14,750
When did I ever hit you?

354
00:24:14,901 --> 00:24:16,667
Tell me, when did I ever hit you?

355
00:24:16,934 --> 00:24:20,634
Tell the truth! Let me go!

356
00:24:21,234 --> 00:24:22,901
Why are you lying?

357
00:24:23,001 --> 00:24:24,501
I never hit you.

358
00:24:24,601 --> 00:24:26,218
Tell the truth!

359
00:24:26,301 --> 00:24:28,134
Say it straight!

360
00:24:28,567 --> 00:24:29,901
Hey!

361
00:24:30,934 --> 00:24:32,467
Let go of me!

362
00:24:33,479 --> 00:24:36,238
You don't have to worry.
I believe in you, Gyu O.

363
00:24:39,834 --> 00:24:42,734
We can't just sit here,
we need to fight back.

364
00:24:42,967 --> 00:24:46,334
We've got connections, too. Just wait.

365
00:24:52,667 --> 00:24:54,467
(Gyu Yeong)

366
00:24:56,534 --> 00:24:57,534
What?

367
00:24:57,701 --> 00:25:02,018
That teacher who adored you in school,
he's Gyu O's vice principal now, right?

368
00:25:02,101 --> 00:25:03,101
So?

369
00:25:03,834 --> 00:25:06,909
Gyu O's bullying hearing is coming up,
so call him first...

370
00:25:06,934 --> 00:25:07,934
No.

371
00:25:08,101 --> 00:25:10,167
You refuse without even hearing me out.

372
00:25:12,801 --> 00:25:16,134
You want me to call and ask him
to go easy on Han Gyu O, don't you?

373
00:25:16,575 --> 00:25:19,018
Why'd he cause trouble again? Is he rich?

374
00:25:19,101 --> 00:25:20,767
Does he have cash to pay settlements?

375
00:25:20,901 --> 00:25:24,430
So you'd walk past a close friend
getting beaten by bullies?

376
00:25:24,534 --> 00:25:26,801
- Would you do that?
- Yeah.

377
00:25:26,901 --> 00:25:29,401
I would. "Friends," please.

378
00:25:29,534 --> 00:25:31,684
There's no such thing as friends now.

379
00:25:31,767 --> 00:25:33,867
And did that friend actually
take Han Gyu O's side?

380
00:25:37,801 --> 00:25:39,801
Forget it. Don't do anything!

381
00:25:39,901 --> 00:25:41,467
Stay out of it!

382
00:25:42,601 --> 00:25:44,984
I was going to stay out of it anyway.

383
00:25:45,067 --> 00:25:47,067
I'm swamped as it is. Bye!

384
00:25:49,834 --> 00:25:51,501
Don't worry about it.

385
00:25:51,734 --> 00:25:55,301
I'll handle my own mess, so don't
bother calling someone like Gyu Yeong.

386
00:25:56,601 --> 00:25:59,267
Either way, hitting someone is wrong.

387
00:25:59,401 --> 00:26:01,401
Even if it's unfair, admit fault.

388
00:26:02,001 --> 00:26:06,834
You've no record, and it was a one-off,
so intent and repetition score zero.

389
00:26:07,134 --> 00:26:11,367
Admit it, show remorse, promise never
again that scores zero, too.

390
00:26:11,834 --> 00:26:16,951
You hit hard and won't reconcile,
so four points each...

391
00:26:17,034 --> 00:26:19,034
Eight total.

392
00:26:19,134 --> 00:26:22,534
You'll likely just get community service.

393
00:26:23,034 --> 00:26:24,651
When did you study all that?

394
00:26:24,734 --> 00:26:27,134
In the taxi on the way to the station.

395
00:26:30,601 --> 00:26:32,118
I'm sorry.

396
00:26:32,143 --> 00:26:34,776
You're struggling, and I piled on...

397
00:26:35,334 --> 00:26:38,160
You beat those kids so badly...

398
00:26:38,667 --> 00:26:41,605
It's not like you did great,
so I can't exactly praise you, but...

399
00:26:43,201 --> 00:26:44,201
Well...

400
00:26:44,367 --> 00:26:47,622
If you'd walked past while Yeong Jun
got beaten like that,

401
00:26:47,647 --> 00:26:50,394
I think that would've bothered me more.

402
00:26:51,601 --> 00:26:52,601
Really?

403
00:26:53,834 --> 00:26:57,234
Yeong Jun didn't
have one spot left unhurt.

404
00:26:57,601 --> 00:27:00,501
How are kids barely 19 so rotten already?

405
00:27:00,667 --> 00:27:04,301
If I'd caught them, they'd be dead today.

406
00:27:08,001 --> 00:27:11,267
Let's just live as it comes.
See what happens. Let's go!

407
00:27:16,501 --> 00:27:18,367
(Gyu Min)

408
00:27:19,634 --> 00:27:20,701
Gyu Min.

409
00:27:21,429 --> 00:27:25,301
Please, stop Gyu Seo.

410
00:27:33,534 --> 00:27:34,534
Over there.

411
00:27:40,398 --> 00:27:42,334
- Gyu Min!
- Han Gyu Seo!

412
00:27:42,359 --> 00:27:43,409
Gyu Min!

413
00:27:43,434 --> 00:27:44,434
Gyu Seo!

414
00:27:44,459 --> 00:27:45,934
Where do you think you're going?

415
00:27:46,183 --> 00:27:47,434
Come on.

416
00:27:51,567 --> 00:27:54,451
Gyu Rim!

417
00:27:54,476 --> 00:27:56,709
Gyu Min, are you okay?

418
00:27:57,867 --> 00:28:00,618
- Where's Gyu Seo?
- Over there!

419
00:28:00,643 --> 00:28:01,643
Let's go!

420
00:28:07,534 --> 00:28:08,601
Gyu Seo!

421
00:28:12,078 --> 00:28:14,218
Gyu Seo, are you okay?

422
00:28:14,301 --> 00:28:17,734
What happened? Why are you kids
at Seoul Station this late at night?

423
00:28:18,064 --> 00:28:24,497
Dong Hui said our mom begs around
Seoul Station like a beggar.

424
00:28:24,834 --> 00:28:31,301
I said it was a lie and not to go,
but Gyu Seo kept insisting...

425
00:28:34,212 --> 00:28:36,745
Do you even know Mom's face?

426
00:28:39,801 --> 00:28:43,201
How will you find her if you don't?

427
00:28:43,931 --> 00:28:48,448
Hey, your mom ran off and left you
when you were just three.

428
00:28:48,840 --> 00:28:51,806
What's the point of finding her?
Come here.

429
00:28:51,986 --> 00:28:53,234
Stop it!

430
00:28:57,501 --> 00:29:00,801
I know what your mom looks like.

431
00:29:01,267 --> 00:29:04,018
If you wait, I'll find her for you.

432
00:29:04,043 --> 00:29:05,401
You don't have to find her.

433
00:29:05,634 --> 00:29:07,867
I don't miss Mom one bit.

434
00:29:07,892 --> 00:29:09,903
But I do.

435
00:29:09,928 --> 00:29:11,637
Hey, are you dumb?

436
00:29:11,662 --> 00:29:15,362
You just don't know how awful Mom is.

437
00:29:15,801 --> 00:29:20,634
- Gyu Min!
- Gyu Seo must be a total idiot.

438
00:29:23,207 --> 00:29:26,407
Don't say that to your brother.

439
00:29:27,281 --> 00:29:29,414
It's okay. Gyu Seo, don't cry.

440
00:29:29,934 --> 00:29:33,451
Gyu Min doesn't mean it. Don't cry.

441
00:29:33,534 --> 00:29:35,401
It's okay, come here.

442
00:29:36,403 --> 00:29:37,490
It's okay.

443
00:29:40,867 --> 00:29:42,801
One disaster at a time, please.

444
00:29:43,201 --> 00:29:46,667
At this rate, our sister's going
to waste away.

445
00:30:15,416 --> 00:30:16,923
You scared me!

446
00:30:18,201 --> 00:30:20,974
Ma'am, let's settle this!

447
00:30:21,454 --> 00:30:23,497
Settle what?

448
00:30:23,604 --> 00:30:27,124
Why would you spread useless rumors
and make Dong Hui repeat them?

449
00:30:27,391 --> 00:30:29,237
Have you ever seen the twins' mom...

450
00:30:29,491 --> 00:30:32,037
I mean, our stepmom,

451
00:30:34,197 --> 00:30:36,044
begging at Seoul Station?

452
00:30:37,230 --> 00:30:39,504
I didn't see it, but I heard about it.

453
00:30:39,529 --> 00:30:40,782
Who told you?

454
00:30:41,191 --> 00:30:43,391
Well... I don't remember.

455
00:30:43,597 --> 00:30:44,915
Was it Suk Hui's mom?

456
00:30:44,989 --> 00:30:47,597
Or was it Mr. Kim?
Or maybe Mi Yeong's grandmother?

457
00:30:48,037 --> 00:30:51,877
I don't remember in detail,
but anyway, I also heard about it.

458
00:30:54,904 --> 00:30:57,667
You don't even remember
where you heard it,

459
00:30:58,068 --> 00:31:00,284
yet you talked like you saw it yourself?

460
00:31:00,984 --> 00:31:04,717
Honestly, she deserves to end up
begging at Seoul Station.

461
00:31:05,251 --> 00:31:07,218
After ruining someone else's family,

462
00:31:07,319 --> 00:31:10,756
she lived there only for three years
and left the twins behind,

463
00:31:10,943 --> 00:31:13,485
- to run off with the accounting manager.
- Ma'am!

464
00:31:13,606 --> 00:31:15,163
It's not like she just ran off.

465
00:31:15,624 --> 00:31:19,092
She cleaned out your family's money
and ran off, leaving you all broke,

466
00:31:19,139 --> 00:31:22,404
Don't you hate her? Don't you resent her?

467
00:31:23,191 --> 00:31:25,159
Those twins she abandoned,

468
00:31:25,253 --> 00:31:27,884
do you really love them
like your own siblings?

469
00:31:28,604 --> 00:31:30,171
Do you have any backbone at all?

470
00:31:30,777 --> 00:31:33,391
If it had been me, I would have...
What are you...?

471
00:31:34,137 --> 00:31:36,511
You must be crazy.

472
00:32:26,017 --> 00:32:27,397
Don't you have anything better to do?

473
00:32:35,604 --> 00:32:37,231
You're not my type.

474
00:32:37,711 --> 00:32:40,247
I've told you I can't stand
women like you,

475
00:32:40,575 --> 00:32:42,244
more times than I can count.

476
00:32:42,684 --> 00:32:44,378
I've warned you countless times.

477
00:32:44,633 --> 00:32:47,657
If I catch you again,
there'll be no mercy.

478
00:32:47,723 --> 00:32:49,055
Mu Jin.

479
00:32:49,257 --> 00:32:51,664
Sorry, but I don't even know you.

480
00:32:53,890 --> 00:32:56,457
Hello, police? I'd like
to report a stalker.

481
00:32:56,482 --> 00:32:58,287
How am I a stalker?

482
00:32:59,611 --> 00:33:01,243
Do you really not know me?

483
00:33:01,744 --> 00:33:04,391
It's me, Seo Hyeon. Jang Seo Hyeon.

484
00:33:04,937 --> 00:33:06,603
Who's Jang Seo Hyeon?

485
00:33:07,371 --> 00:33:08,642
Hello?

486
00:33:09,383 --> 00:33:13,771
Are you really Seo Hyeon? No way...

487
00:33:14,791 --> 00:33:16,537
Hey, how could that be you?

488
00:33:18,137 --> 00:33:19,664
I didn't recognize you.

489
00:33:22,837 --> 00:33:24,644
Why not?

490
00:33:30,110 --> 00:33:32,737
Seo Hyeon, it's been so long. Goodness.

491
00:33:32,750 --> 00:33:33,750
Chairwoman.

492
00:33:33,784 --> 00:33:35,684
It's been ages.

493
00:33:37,676 --> 00:33:41,177
So you almost got reported as a stalker?

494
00:33:41,611 --> 00:33:43,697
I never imagined it was Seo Hyeon.

495
00:33:44,244 --> 00:33:46,657
Do you really have that many stalkers?

496
00:33:46,864 --> 00:33:48,264
There are a few.

497
00:33:48,670 --> 00:33:50,778
Still, how could you not recognize me?

498
00:33:50,957 --> 00:33:52,124
Am I really that ugly?

499
00:33:53,190 --> 00:33:54,190
That's not it.

500
00:33:54,211 --> 00:33:56,764
Stalkers look normal too,

501
00:33:56,791 --> 00:33:58,697
and that's the problem.

502
00:33:58,764 --> 00:34:00,338
Goodness,

503
00:34:00,599 --> 00:34:04,394
I think the last time I saw you
was before you studied abroad.

504
00:34:04,449 --> 00:34:05,670
You graduated already?

505
00:34:05,717 --> 00:34:08,204
Yes. I graduated and got a job as well.

506
00:34:08,911 --> 00:34:12,564
How have you been, Chairwoman?
Sorry for greeting you so late.

507
00:34:13,044 --> 00:34:15,331
Seo Hyeon, you've become so beautiful.

508
00:34:15,356 --> 00:34:17,397
Your baby fat is all gone.

509
00:34:17,731 --> 00:34:20,179
I wouldn't recognize you on the street.

510
00:34:20,547 --> 00:34:21,571
You must be dating someone, right?

511
00:34:22,964 --> 00:34:24,997
I really wish I were,

512
00:34:25,291 --> 00:34:27,796
I sent tons of emails and messages,

513
00:34:27,890 --> 00:34:29,204
but he never even responds.

514
00:34:29,284 --> 00:34:30,451
He just calls me a stalker.

515
00:34:33,664 --> 00:34:36,743
I'll head upstairs, take a shower,
and get changed.

516
00:34:37,031 --> 00:34:38,057
See you later.

517
00:34:41,921 --> 00:34:44,811
Mu Jin has become even grumpier
than before.

518
00:34:45,757 --> 00:34:48,957
Business training has him
on edge these days.

519
00:34:50,371 --> 00:34:52,250
Shall we go inside and talk?

520
00:34:54,637 --> 00:34:56,643
He doesn't seem like an easy target,

521
00:34:56,911 --> 00:34:59,117
wouldn't it be better
to find someone else?

522
00:34:59,604 --> 00:35:02,650
It's okay.
Easy guys aren't my type either.

523
00:35:02,657 --> 00:35:04,497
I like a challenge.

524
00:35:06,950 --> 00:35:10,413
I know I'm far from the daughter-in-law
you deserve,

525
00:35:10,421 --> 00:35:13,297
so I'll do better and try even harder.

526
00:35:15,630 --> 00:35:18,504
It's been so long.
Don't you think that's too forward?

527
00:35:18,664 --> 00:35:20,117
Chairwoman.

528
00:35:22,357 --> 00:35:23,410
Seo Hyeon,

529
00:35:23,497 --> 00:35:24,752
a few days ago,

530
00:35:24,773 --> 00:35:27,137
I saw your father at a business gathering.

531
00:35:27,577 --> 00:35:28,777
Yes, I heard.

532
00:35:29,890 --> 00:35:31,957
You and your mom get along, right?

533
00:35:32,404 --> 00:35:33,577
Of course.

534
00:35:33,751 --> 00:35:35,976
I feel bad saying this
about my late mother,

535
00:35:36,003 --> 00:35:38,624
but I love my mom now ten times more.

536
00:35:55,591 --> 00:35:56,604
I'm heading in.

537
00:36:25,051 --> 00:36:26,830
Then close your eyes,

538
00:36:26,911 --> 00:36:30,597
breathe deep, and cast the spell inside.

539
00:36:31,357 --> 00:36:32,802
Close your eyes.

540
00:36:33,730 --> 00:36:36,331
It's nothing. It's no big deal.

541
00:36:36,777 --> 00:36:38,263
See if I give you an inch of my heart,

542
00:36:38,264 --> 00:36:40,064
or memory.

543
00:36:40,411 --> 00:36:42,004
Act up all you want.

544
00:36:42,290 --> 00:36:46,091
See if a single hair or lash
of mine even twitches.

545
00:36:46,824 --> 00:36:48,162
Now open your eyes,

546
00:36:48,230 --> 00:36:50,604
and do it with a big smile.

547
00:36:58,117 --> 00:37:01,304
You scared me! When did you come in?

548
00:37:01,329 --> 00:37:03,097
I knocked several times,

549
00:37:03,104 --> 00:37:06,204
what were you so focused on?
A puzzle cube?

550
00:37:06,417 --> 00:37:07,790
Why the sudden interest?

551
00:37:09,224 --> 00:37:11,047
I saw a girl who was really good at it,

552
00:37:11,049 --> 00:37:12,064
and she looked so cool.

553
00:37:12,131 --> 00:37:13,350
Who is she?

554
00:37:14,130 --> 00:37:15,137
Han Gyu Rim.

555
00:37:15,162 --> 00:37:17,675
Han Gyu Rim? Who's Han Gyu Rim?

556
00:37:18,157 --> 00:37:19,171
Someone.

557
00:37:19,631 --> 00:37:20,730
The woman you like?

558
00:37:22,131 --> 00:37:24,731
I don't know if I like her,
but I can't stop thinking of her.

559
00:37:24,891 --> 00:37:26,451
Then you do like her.

560
00:37:27,957 --> 00:37:30,871
Really? It's only been one day.

561
00:37:30,896 --> 00:37:32,691
Why would you need time to like someone?

562
00:37:32,704 --> 00:37:34,757
People can fall in love
in just ten seconds.

563
00:37:36,464 --> 00:37:39,391
Even so, one day seems too soon.

564
00:37:42,144 --> 00:37:43,599
What does she do?

565
00:37:43,760 --> 00:37:45,268
Is she prettier than me?

566
00:37:45,676 --> 00:37:46,777
What school does she go to?

567
00:37:46,877 --> 00:37:48,224
What do her parents do?

568
00:37:48,957 --> 00:37:52,304
Am I really the type
to fall for someone so easily?

569
00:37:53,124 --> 00:37:54,343
Mu Jin,

570
00:37:55,744 --> 00:37:59,504
how could you tell me
you like another woman?

571
00:38:00,237 --> 00:38:01,970
Me? When?

572
00:38:03,823 --> 00:38:06,451
No. That can't be.

573
00:38:07,344 --> 00:38:09,577
That's impossible, it can't be true.

574
00:38:13,523 --> 00:38:18,213
I'm going for a walk.
Hang out a little longer.

575
00:38:18,724 --> 00:38:19,744
Mu Jin.

576
00:38:19,771 --> 00:38:20,791
I'll eat this and go.

577
00:38:23,024 --> 00:38:24,183
Mu Jin.

578
00:38:29,471 --> 00:38:33,464
No, it can't be.

579
00:38:44,057 --> 00:38:45,917
What are you doing?

580
00:38:47,418 --> 00:38:49,891
Well, I'm just curious,

581
00:38:49,951 --> 00:38:51,610
it's okay to ask when you're curious.

582
00:38:54,631 --> 00:38:56,330
Nothing happened, right?

583
00:38:56,677 --> 00:38:58,504
Sleep well. See you tomorrow.

584
00:39:03,424 --> 00:39:05,913
Isn't "sleep well"
a little too much already?

585
00:39:07,374 --> 00:39:08,464
Yeah, that's too much.

586
00:39:08,551 --> 00:39:11,717
Nothing happened, right? See you tomorrow.

587
00:39:11,938 --> 00:39:13,224
No.

588
00:39:13,951 --> 00:39:16,825
Then why even ask if something happened?

589
00:39:17,992 --> 00:39:19,217
See you tomorrow.

590
00:39:21,797 --> 00:39:24,797
Why would I suddenly say,
"See you tomorrow?"

591
00:39:27,237 --> 00:39:28,377
Hello?

592
00:39:33,711 --> 00:39:34,717
Hello?

593
00:39:36,070 --> 00:39:37,577
Hello, this is Kim Mu Jin.

594
00:39:38,444 --> 00:39:39,939
Mu Jin,

595
00:39:40,767 --> 00:39:42,931
what brings you to call so late?

596
00:39:46,411 --> 00:39:49,577
I was worried
after the way you left earlier,

597
00:39:50,710 --> 00:39:53,144
so I got your number from the manager.

598
00:39:54,871 --> 00:39:55,884
Yes.

599
00:40:01,404 --> 00:40:04,150
I hope it wasn't something
that made you drink cocoa.

600
00:40:07,871 --> 00:40:08,891
Yes.

601
00:40:12,677 --> 00:40:15,064
I don't know what happened,

602
00:40:16,831 --> 00:40:20,177
but I hope everything works out.

603
00:40:21,624 --> 00:40:23,897
Sleep well. See you tomorrow.

604
00:40:25,357 --> 00:40:30,184
Yes, thank you.
Sleep well. See you tomorrow.

605
00:40:30,931 --> 00:40:31,951
Yes.

606
00:40:41,297 --> 00:40:44,150
That wasn't bad. It felt natural.

607
00:40:44,371 --> 00:40:46,304
Well done.

608
00:40:49,291 --> 00:40:53,844
So now what? What will you do now, Mu Jin?

609
00:40:54,671 --> 00:40:57,670
Don't tell me you're thinking
of confessing to her.

610
00:40:58,604 --> 00:40:59,631
That's not it.

611
00:40:59,671 --> 00:41:03,154
I barely know Han Gyu Rim.

612
00:41:03,334 --> 00:41:05,263
No way. Not now or ever.

613
00:41:06,170 --> 00:41:07,257
Who knows what'll happen.

614
00:41:07,282 --> 00:41:08,490
What do you mean, "Who knows?"

615
00:42:01,604 --> 00:42:04,957
It's tiring, but it's manageable.

616
00:42:04,982 --> 00:42:07,409
So you're like an undercover boss?

617
00:42:08,324 --> 00:42:09,397
Maybe...

618
00:42:15,431 --> 00:42:17,984
Han Gyu Min,
you picked out the beans again?

619
00:42:18,317 --> 00:42:20,995
Gyu Min's got her recorder today.

620
00:42:21,036 --> 00:42:22,044
Jump rope.

621
00:42:22,050 --> 00:42:23,564
Yes! Go get your jump rope.

622
00:42:24,304 --> 00:42:25,831
I don't like it. It's not pretty.

623
00:42:25,844 --> 00:42:27,397
How about we do it on both sides?

624
00:42:28,944 --> 00:42:30,142
Listen to your teacher,

625
00:42:30,149 --> 00:42:32,371
don't fight with your friends,
and watch for cars.

626
00:42:32,431 --> 00:42:33,504
Have a good day.

627
00:43:52,924 --> 00:43:54,108
- I'll get going.
- Okay.

628
00:43:54,133 --> 00:43:55,135
Yes.

629
00:44:13,751 --> 00:44:15,117
Do you live around here?

630
00:44:15,337 --> 00:44:16,437
No.

631
00:44:17,165 --> 00:44:18,611
Actually, yes.

632
00:44:26,311 --> 00:44:28,337
People will think we're really dating.

633
00:44:30,210 --> 00:44:31,237
That's right.

634
00:44:51,701 --> 00:44:54,151
- Sit down.
- Mu Jin, you sit down.

635
00:44:54,870 --> 00:44:56,477
I like standing.

636
00:44:57,790 --> 00:44:58,810
Thank you.

637
00:45:03,797 --> 00:45:05,044
Give me your bag.

638
00:45:06,124 --> 00:45:07,624
- I'm fine.
- Give it to me.

639
00:45:09,931 --> 00:45:10,944
Thank you.

640
00:45:29,770 --> 00:45:30,824
I could've done that.

641
00:45:30,844 --> 00:45:32,397
I just can't ignore things like that.

642
00:45:33,644 --> 00:45:34,937
Thank you.

643
00:45:39,171 --> 00:45:40,744
It was untied last time too.

644
00:46:09,330 --> 00:46:11,270
You're making it way too obvious.

645
00:46:14,111 --> 00:46:16,877
Mu Jin, let's be careful.

646
00:46:24,251 --> 00:46:26,624
- Yes.
- Do you have 10,000 dollars?

647
00:46:26,931 --> 00:46:28,823
What kind of question
is that out of nowhere?

648
00:46:28,898 --> 00:46:30,084
Do you have it or not?

649
00:46:30,151 --> 00:46:31,680
Why do you suddenly need 10,000 dollars?

650
00:46:31,681 --> 00:46:33,544
Do you have it or not? Just answer.

651
00:46:33,671 --> 00:46:36,056
Why would I have that kind of money?

652
00:46:37,030 --> 00:46:38,270
You really don't?

653
00:46:38,324 --> 00:46:40,480
You work from dawn till late at night,

654
00:46:40,608 --> 00:46:42,017
and you don't have 10,000 dollars?

655
00:46:42,777 --> 00:46:44,647
Are you just lying
because you won't lend it?

656
00:46:44,648 --> 00:46:45,664
I don't.

657
00:46:45,691 --> 00:46:48,615
My paycheck barely covers
our family of six.

658
00:46:48,763 --> 00:46:49,791
Fine. Bye.

659
00:47:01,951 --> 00:47:03,797
What a jerk.

660
00:47:04,777 --> 00:47:06,526
If you're not giving me money, shut up.

661
00:47:07,773 --> 00:47:09,717
What a temper.

662
00:47:13,224 --> 00:47:16,571
Hey, don't do this.
Why don't you just ask your mom?

663
00:47:17,319 --> 00:47:18,789
I told you already.

664
00:47:18,904 --> 00:47:22,544
Your mom remarried
Chairman Jang Hun Tae of Seonga Apparel.

665
00:47:23,109 --> 00:47:25,337
Chairman Jang and my uncle are friends,

666
00:47:25,362 --> 00:47:28,782
and I saw your mom in his photos.

667
00:47:29,791 --> 00:47:31,349
Your mom's Cinderella story,

668
00:47:31,403 --> 00:47:33,564
everyone in that circle knows about it.

669
00:47:36,291 --> 00:47:38,021
She's probably busy living her own life,

670
00:47:38,076 --> 00:47:39,704
and just forgot about us.

671
00:47:39,844 --> 00:47:43,033
Even if she's married
into a wealthy family,

672
00:47:43,080 --> 00:47:44,404
you're just going to ignore it?

673
00:47:44,464 --> 00:47:47,204
After her husband cheated
and her life fell apart,

674
00:47:47,884 --> 00:47:49,684
she probably wanted
to leave it all behind.

675
00:47:50,251 --> 00:47:52,737
If she wanted to see us,
she would've come already.

676
00:47:54,084 --> 00:47:55,924
Would she even have had time
to contact you?

677
00:47:56,371 --> 00:47:57,657
She stayed in America
for her daughter's education,

678
00:47:57,691 --> 00:48:00,612
and came back recently.

679
00:48:01,193 --> 00:48:03,244
Daughter? What daughter?

680
00:48:04,557 --> 00:48:06,764
The chairman's daughter
from his late wife.

681
00:48:07,291 --> 00:48:09,617
Your mom raised her like her own daughter.

682
00:48:12,952 --> 00:48:15,284
Anyway, you go talk to her.

683
00:48:15,791 --> 00:48:17,977
Tell her you're not trying
to break up her family.

684
00:48:18,002 --> 00:48:19,521
Just borrow some money.

685
00:48:20,441 --> 00:48:22,688
If her own child asks for money to study,

686
00:48:23,259 --> 00:48:24,824
you think she'd say no?

687
00:48:27,764 --> 00:48:30,724
If Gyu Rim finds out I went to Mom,
she'll kill me.

688
00:48:30,930 --> 00:48:33,017
She's usually such a softie,

689
00:48:33,171 --> 00:48:36,204
but once she snaps, she's terrifying.

690
00:48:37,231 --> 00:48:40,344
There's a rabid dog
living inside Han Gyu Rim.

691
00:48:53,230 --> 00:48:54,237
Seo Hyeon.

692
00:48:54,244 --> 00:48:57,444
Mom, did you have a good trip?

693
00:48:57,544 --> 00:48:59,397
I'm sorry I couldn't go meet you
at the airport.

694
00:49:00,184 --> 00:49:01,684
Were things okay in Seoul
while we were away?

695
00:49:01,704 --> 00:49:03,180
Of course.

696
00:49:03,194 --> 00:49:05,871
Happy anniversary, Mom.

697
00:49:05,885 --> 00:49:07,584
Oh my goodness!

698
00:49:08,144 --> 00:49:10,964
Baby's breath! My favorite flowers.

699
00:49:11,064 --> 00:49:12,640
- Thank you.
- Where's Dad's gift?

700
00:49:13,128 --> 00:49:15,111
Did she get married alone? Give it to me.

701
00:49:15,597 --> 00:49:18,590
Hang on. I got something for you too.

702
00:49:18,637 --> 00:49:19,637
Hurry up.

703
00:49:19,662 --> 00:49:21,268
This one's for Mom.

704
00:49:21,451 --> 00:49:24,204
And this one's for Mom too.

705
00:49:25,510 --> 00:49:27,200
I'll throw away all your presents.

706
00:49:27,701 --> 00:49:29,377
You're so unfair.

707
00:49:30,597 --> 00:49:32,269
- But wait a second.
- What?

708
00:49:32,577 --> 00:49:35,660
Why do you look so worn out?

709
00:49:36,956 --> 00:49:39,984
You skipped meals again
while I was gone, didn't you?

710
00:49:40,171 --> 00:49:43,684
I left plenty of food
ready to heat up in the fridge.

711
00:49:43,757 --> 00:49:45,481
She's on a diet.

712
00:49:45,711 --> 00:49:48,031
Mom, what's this spot?
I don't remember it.

713
00:49:48,097 --> 00:49:49,574
Did you not wear enough sunscreen?

714
00:49:50,769 --> 00:49:51,991
I'm fine.

715
00:49:52,090 --> 00:49:55,690
I told you, skipping meals isn't healthy.

716
00:49:55,870 --> 00:49:57,819
- This won't do.
- Don't you see Dad's tan?

717
00:49:57,844 --> 00:49:59,712
Mom, it's a good thing you got divorced.

718
00:50:00,144 --> 00:50:02,637
Your life's turned around completely.

719
00:50:03,131 --> 00:50:05,917
- Mom, what do I do?
- So unfair.

720
00:50:09,712 --> 00:50:10,865
(Se Hee, did you look into
what I asked about last time?)

721
00:50:10,874 --> 00:50:12,106
(Yeah, hold on.)
(Chairman Jang Hun Tae, 010-0575-4228)

722
00:50:57,691 --> 00:50:58,811
Han Gyu Yeong?

723
00:51:05,851 --> 00:51:08,150
You really resemble your mother.

724
00:51:08,197 --> 00:51:09,230
By any chance, my Mom, I mean,

725
00:51:11,024 --> 00:51:14,397
didn't your wife mention our existence?

726
00:51:15,044 --> 00:51:16,075
Yes,

727
00:51:16,956 --> 00:51:17,982
she did.

728
00:51:18,183 --> 00:51:21,631
She divorced and left three kids, right?

729
00:51:21,937 --> 00:51:22,938
Yes.

730
00:51:23,893 --> 00:51:24,998
What a relief.

731
00:51:25,793 --> 00:51:27,756
I was worried I'd cause trouble...

732
00:51:27,758 --> 00:51:30,290
in Mom's happy family.
I was really terrified.

733
00:51:34,364 --> 00:51:36,384
It's a bit awkward,

734
00:51:37,071 --> 00:51:40,524
but I'm also curious why you called.

735
00:51:42,191 --> 00:51:44,697
How did you get my number?

736
00:51:46,571 --> 00:51:49,607
- So you've kept in touch with Mom?
- Mom,

737
00:51:50,708 --> 00:51:53,068
I mean, I haven't been in touch
with your wife.

738
00:51:53,070 --> 00:51:54,511
I don't even know her number.

739
00:51:55,451 --> 00:51:57,137
Your number,

740
00:51:57,139 --> 00:51:59,164
I got it through my friend's uncle.

741
00:51:59,257 --> 00:52:01,291
That you and my Mom remarried,

742
00:52:02,105 --> 00:52:03,897
I heard that through that friend long ago.

743
00:52:04,411 --> 00:52:05,437
I see.

744
00:52:08,851 --> 00:52:11,144
I'll get straight to the point.

745
00:52:11,557 --> 00:52:13,790
If you think I'm a total bum,

746
00:52:14,231 --> 00:52:15,650
feel free to walk away.

747
00:52:16,144 --> 00:52:17,164
Okay.

748
00:52:19,257 --> 00:52:20,730
Please lend me some money.

749
00:52:24,211 --> 00:52:25,769
As you can see,

750
00:52:25,771 --> 00:52:27,423
I go to the same med school,

751
00:52:27,425 --> 00:52:28,904
you graduated from.

752
00:52:29,457 --> 00:52:32,206
I bombed my midterms this time,

753
00:52:32,653 --> 00:52:34,497
and lost my scholarship.

754
00:52:35,276 --> 00:52:37,809
So next semester's tuition
is really stressing me out.

755
00:52:38,444 --> 00:52:39,601
If you lend it to me,

756
00:52:39,995 --> 00:52:41,697
I'll pay you back with interest.

757
00:52:49,891 --> 00:52:51,697
Send me your account number by text.

758
00:52:52,437 --> 00:52:54,511
I'll send you the tuition.

759
00:52:54,850 --> 00:52:56,524
And you don't need to pay me back.

760
00:52:56,897 --> 00:52:58,843
If you're my wife's daughter,

761
00:52:58,845 --> 00:53:00,920
you're like my own child.

762
00:53:01,068 --> 00:53:02,084
I see.

763
00:53:04,804 --> 00:53:06,110
Thank you.

764
00:53:09,497 --> 00:53:10,804
Thank you so much.

765
00:53:13,542 --> 00:53:15,502
(Chairman Jang Hun Tae,
Daehan Bank 65090204-09)

766
00:53:20,984 --> 00:53:23,897
Yes, I'll send it right away.

767
00:53:24,690 --> 00:53:27,348
This is for you!

768
00:53:27,351 --> 00:53:31,210
I said you'll ruin your health
if you keep skipping meals.

769
00:53:35,030 --> 00:53:36,608
But now that I think about it,

770
00:53:37,276 --> 00:53:39,817
I don't think I need
to be this submissive.

771
00:53:40,918 --> 00:53:43,533
- What?
- Regardless of circumstances,

772
00:53:43,535 --> 00:53:46,004
I lost my mom,
and so did my sister and brother.

773
00:53:46,885 --> 00:53:48,310
Thanks to that, Chairman,

774
00:53:48,958 --> 00:53:51,031
you got a mom for your daughter.

775
00:53:53,537 --> 00:53:54,615
I'll think of it as compensation,

776
00:53:55,883 --> 00:53:58,137
consolation money. I'll use it well.

777
00:54:04,110 --> 00:54:05,150
Excuse me.

778
00:54:07,791 --> 00:54:09,457
Don't you want to see your mom?

779
00:54:10,057 --> 00:54:11,077
No.

780
00:54:11,578 --> 00:54:12,624
Not really.

781
00:54:13,510 --> 00:54:14,577
I see.

782
00:54:16,577 --> 00:54:19,187
I'd appreciate it if you didn't mention,

783
00:54:19,501 --> 00:54:21,626
meeting me or giving me money.

784
00:54:23,154 --> 00:54:24,170
Goodbye.

785
00:54:41,804 --> 00:54:43,017
Hey,

786
00:54:45,498 --> 00:54:46,924
are you looking for someone?

787
00:54:48,884 --> 00:54:49,924
Yes.

788
00:54:53,511 --> 00:54:57,217
- Go inside and look.
- No, that's not it.

789
00:55:00,957 --> 00:55:02,855
Are you here to eat?

790
00:55:02,857 --> 00:55:04,635
No, I'm not here to eat, just,

791
00:55:04,637 --> 00:55:07,104
I'll just stand here a bit and leave.

792
00:55:12,836 --> 00:55:15,003
Wait, don't go. Stay here.

793
00:55:26,877 --> 00:55:27,905
Hey,

794
00:55:31,779 --> 00:55:34,017
here's my lunch box. Please eat it.

795
00:55:34,051 --> 00:55:35,704
My lunch isn't settling well.

796
00:55:38,301 --> 00:55:39,901
(Han Gyu Rim)

797
00:55:41,850 --> 00:55:42,868
No, I can't.

798
00:55:43,156 --> 00:55:44,711
It's not that, here,

799
00:55:45,674 --> 00:55:46,683
Hey!

800
00:55:47,371 --> 00:55:48,811
It's fine, just eat it.

801
00:55:57,184 --> 00:56:03,237
<i>Happy birthday to you</i>

802
00:56:03,357 --> 00:56:04,367
What?

803
00:56:04,768 --> 00:56:07,417
How can someone be so adorable?

804
00:56:08,297 --> 00:56:10,536
Kind, cute...

805
00:56:11,790 --> 00:56:14,537
and pretty too? That's unbelievable.

806
00:56:16,257 --> 00:56:17,604
Did you get scammed?

807
00:56:19,284 --> 00:56:21,105
Why are you standing outside? Go in.

808
00:56:21,686 --> 00:56:22,698
Mu Jin.

809
00:56:22,998 --> 00:56:25,007
- What?
- Han Gyu Rim?

810
00:56:25,688 --> 00:56:28,011
- What about Han Gyu Rim?
- Do you know Han Gyu Rim?

811
00:56:29,631 --> 00:56:31,928
I know one Han Gyu Rim. Why?

812
00:56:31,930 --> 00:56:34,417
That Han Gyu Rim
is right there, isn't she?

813
00:56:38,011 --> 00:56:39,025
Why?

814
00:56:39,786 --> 00:56:42,011
- Thanks.
- Dude, what's wrong?

815
00:56:42,271 --> 00:56:44,303
Mu Jin, that Han Gyu Rim,

816
00:56:45,464 --> 00:56:46,504
introduce me to her.

817
00:56:50,217 --> 00:56:51,710
Which Han Gyu Rim?

818
00:56:52,058 --> 00:56:53,484
What Han Gyu Rim?

819
00:56:54,151 --> 00:56:56,784
The one right there. The one you know.

820
00:56:59,611 --> 00:57:03,317
Then I'll bring a glass of wine
and orange juice right away.

821
00:57:05,251 --> 00:57:07,831
What did Han Gyu Rim do to you?

822
00:57:08,337 --> 00:57:09,905
She fed me when I was starving.

823
00:57:10,460 --> 00:57:12,404
- What?
- So...

824
00:57:14,431 --> 00:57:15,819
I fell for her at first sight.

825
00:57:17,707 --> 00:57:20,687
- Are you starving?
- Please introduce me, bro.

826
00:57:21,828 --> 00:57:22,870
No.

827
00:57:23,311 --> 00:57:25,569
- No? Why not?
- I don't want to.

828
00:57:25,571 --> 00:57:27,007
Why?

829
00:57:28,468 --> 00:57:29,964
What's that?

830
00:57:31,164 --> 00:57:33,009
- Did Han Gyu Rim give you this?
- Yeah.

831
00:57:33,011 --> 00:57:35,076
- Give it here!
- Freeze.

832
00:57:35,078 --> 00:57:36,717
Quiet, get inside.

833
00:57:45,557 --> 00:57:47,237
Why aren't you going in?

834
00:57:49,677 --> 00:57:50,690
Gyu Rim,

835
00:57:53,211 --> 00:57:54,304
let's have a drink.

836
00:57:54,671 --> 00:57:56,210
You're in high school...

837
00:57:58,818 --> 00:58:00,417
Did something happen?

838
00:58:06,864 --> 00:58:07,877
Here.

839
00:58:22,531 --> 00:58:23,897
I'm thinking of dropping out.

840
00:58:26,190 --> 00:58:27,804
They say it's all my fault,

841
00:58:29,190 --> 00:58:33,017
that I should just admit I was wrong,
apologize, and they'll let it go.

842
00:58:33,864 --> 00:58:35,324
I don't want to.

843
00:58:35,957 --> 00:58:37,417
Why should I?

844
00:58:39,177 --> 00:58:40,607
Then don't.

845
00:58:41,041 --> 00:58:42,264
Let's fight instead.

846
00:58:42,677 --> 00:58:44,317
I'll fight with you.

847
00:58:48,057 --> 00:58:50,517
Are you coming to my school with a bat?

848
00:58:52,397 --> 00:58:53,824
I should've just walked past.

849
00:58:54,124 --> 00:58:57,126
Everyone pretends not to see.
What was I supposed to do?

850
00:58:57,794 --> 00:58:58,906
I regret it.

851
00:58:59,493 --> 00:59:01,017
I regret it so much.

852
00:59:01,124 --> 00:59:02,503
Don't regret it.

853
00:59:03,091 --> 00:59:04,710
I said you did the right thing.

854
00:59:05,711 --> 00:59:06,850
That bastard is the bad one.

855
00:59:10,051 --> 00:59:12,104
You just need to hold
on a bit longer to graduate.

856
00:59:13,971 --> 00:59:15,997
I'm not saying I'll give up everything.

857
00:59:16,451 --> 00:59:19,597
Even if I leave school,
I'll study on my own...

858
00:59:19,771 --> 00:59:21,124
and pass the exam.
I'll go to college too, Gyu Rim.

859
00:59:22,371 --> 00:59:23,395
Just a little,

860
00:59:23,929 --> 00:59:26,811
let's think about us a little more, Gyu O.

861
00:59:28,771 --> 00:59:30,631
What more is there to think about?

862
00:59:33,044 --> 00:59:35,811
A guy who can't even handle that much
and wants to drop out,

863
00:59:35,813 --> 00:59:39,316
and the one who, instead of stopping him,
just pats him on the back...

864
00:59:39,457 --> 00:59:40,477
Hey, Han Gyu O,

865
00:59:40,744 --> 00:59:42,622
If you drop out now,
you'll be a middle school grad.

866
00:59:42,624 --> 00:59:44,529
Han Gyu Rim, a high school grad.
Han Gyu O, a middle school grad.

867
00:59:44,531 --> 00:59:47,977
What's the use of going to med school,
grad school, and getting a PhD?

868
00:59:48,317 --> 00:59:50,171
what's the point? You two drag down
the family average.

869
00:59:50,231 --> 00:59:53,224
People ask what your father does,
what your sister does,

870
00:59:53,226 --> 00:59:54,846
what your brother does.
They judge the family so much.

871
00:59:54,871 --> 00:59:58,482
Hey, in all this,
you only think of yourself?

872
00:59:58,485 --> 01:00:01,076
If I don't think of me, who will?

873
01:00:01,077 --> 01:00:05,211
You're only treated with any respect
because of me.

874
01:00:06,204 --> 01:00:08,617
If no one were watching,
I'd throw you away.

875
01:00:10,891 --> 01:00:14,518
Is that how you talk as an older sister?

876
01:00:15,013 --> 01:00:16,751
Seriously.

877
01:00:16,797 --> 01:00:18,589
It's not even something I'm wrong about!

878
01:00:18,591 --> 01:00:19,948
You don't even have 10,000 dollars!

879
01:00:19,951 --> 01:00:22,204
Did you leave 10,000 dollars with me?

880
01:00:22,298 --> 01:00:24,724
That's it, I've had it with you!

881
01:00:25,013 --> 01:00:26,684
- Hey, let go!
- What are you doing?

882
01:00:26,692 --> 01:00:27,824
- Let go!
- Stop it!

883
01:00:27,827 --> 01:00:30,509
- Let go!
- You let go first!

884
01:00:30,510 --> 01:00:31,550
Stop it!

885
01:00:31,552 --> 01:00:34,334
- I said let go!
- Hey, Han Gyu Yeong, you let go!

886
01:00:34,336 --> 01:00:35,551
- Hey!
- I said you let go!

887
01:00:35,553 --> 01:00:37,531
- Don't!
- Han Gyu Yeong, you let go!

888
01:00:37,539 --> 01:00:40,209
- You let go!
- I said let go!

889
01:00:40,438 --> 01:00:41,942
I said you let go!

890
01:00:41,944 --> 01:00:44,862
This family is a real mess.

891
01:00:44,864 --> 01:00:46,511
Let go of each other right now!

892
01:00:53,171 --> 01:00:55,511
What are you sisters doing?

893
01:00:56,917 --> 01:00:58,824
This is why people...

894
01:00:58,826 --> 01:01:01,824
point fingers and say
you're kids with no parents.

895
01:01:05,197 --> 01:01:06,222
Move.

896
01:01:06,843 --> 01:01:09,024
Your father is talking to you!

897
01:01:12,071 --> 01:01:13,322
You twins over there,

898
01:01:13,610 --> 01:01:15,018
aren't you going to greet me?

899
01:01:21,871 --> 01:01:23,204
When did you get here?

900
01:01:23,264 --> 01:01:25,608
How did you raise these kids...

901
01:01:25,644 --> 01:01:28,297
that they all turned out like this?

902
01:01:28,824 --> 01:01:31,590
Did I come here to beg?

903
01:01:31,711 --> 01:01:34,411
It's been a really long time
since you last came home.

904
01:01:35,564 --> 01:01:37,289
With the house in this state,

905
01:01:37,577 --> 01:01:39,417
do you think I'd want to come home?

906
01:01:42,991 --> 01:01:45,266
Compared to how you abandoned us,

907
01:01:45,340 --> 01:01:47,811
we're doing pretty great.

908
01:01:49,417 --> 01:01:50,828
Abandoned?

909
01:01:51,843 --> 01:01:53,924
You think I stayed away for fun?

910
01:01:54,457 --> 01:01:56,583
I was preparing a business, raising funds,

911
01:01:56,584 --> 01:01:59,424
giving presentations, scouting factories.

912
01:02:01,157 --> 01:02:03,296
To give you all a better life,

913
01:02:03,397 --> 01:02:06,031
father was working so hard,
and you don't even know.

914
01:02:09,364 --> 01:02:10,804
Dating again?

915
01:02:15,971 --> 01:02:19,217
- When did this happen?
- After being fooled so many times?

916
01:02:22,051 --> 01:02:23,610
This time is different.

917
01:02:24,623 --> 01:02:25,910
Ms. Cho is the real deal.

918
01:02:26,097 --> 01:02:27,912
If this business works out,

919
01:02:28,806 --> 01:02:30,321
I'll bring her in as your mother.

920
01:02:30,789 --> 01:02:32,251
A house needs a woman,

921
01:02:32,351 --> 01:02:34,004
kids need a mother.

922
01:02:35,097 --> 01:02:36,417
Look at this house,

923
01:02:36,524 --> 01:02:38,411
what in the world is this mess?

924
01:03:21,924 --> 01:03:23,017
Good afternoon.

925
01:03:24,524 --> 01:03:26,017
Good afternoon indeed.

926
01:03:27,664 --> 01:03:28,704
Three days in a row.

927
01:03:30,131 --> 01:03:31,311
I know, right?

928
01:03:32,664 --> 01:03:33,717
Did you drink cocoa?

929
01:03:41,231 --> 01:03:42,444
Is something wrong?

930
01:03:42,857 --> 01:03:43,871
No.

931
01:03:45,106 --> 01:03:46,855
Where in this neighborhood do you live?

932
01:03:46,857 --> 01:03:49,137
I've never seen you around here before.

933
01:03:53,657 --> 01:03:54,742
Well,

934
01:03:55,243 --> 01:03:56,515
further inside...

935
01:03:57,189 --> 01:03:58,217
I see.

936
01:04:05,011 --> 01:04:06,211
Look over here, miss!

937
01:04:09,611 --> 01:04:11,948
- Who are you?
- My mother,

938
01:04:11,951 --> 01:04:13,930
she collapsed at the bus stop...

939
01:04:14,591 --> 01:04:17,529
Right. Is she okay?

940
01:04:17,531 --> 01:04:19,436
Yes, thanks to you,

941
01:04:19,438 --> 01:04:21,849
she had ribs this morning.

942
01:04:21,851 --> 01:04:23,122
She's much better now.

943
01:04:23,124 --> 01:04:24,897
What brings you here?

944
01:04:26,011 --> 01:04:30,374
You disappeared like an angel back then,

945
01:04:30,475 --> 01:04:33,311
I had a really hard time finding you.

946
01:04:33,911 --> 01:04:36,618
I felt it from the first time I saw you,

947
01:04:36,826 --> 01:04:38,008
I thought you were...

948
01:04:38,476 --> 01:04:41,104
an angel descending from the distant sky.

949
01:04:41,857 --> 01:04:43,379
You were so dazzling,

950
01:04:43,408 --> 01:04:45,312
even now, thinking of that moment,

951
01:04:45,433 --> 01:04:47,557
I still can't open my eyes.

952
01:04:47,931 --> 01:04:50,802
If your eyes bother you,
see an eye doctor.

953
01:04:51,616 --> 01:04:52,631
Who are you?

954
01:04:53,011 --> 01:04:55,224
He works with me.

955
01:04:55,824 --> 01:04:56,827
Is that so?

956
01:04:57,334 --> 01:05:00,045
I have something important
to tell Gyu Rim,

957
01:05:00,046 --> 01:05:02,524
could you excuse us for a moment?

958
01:05:06,451 --> 01:05:09,517
We're already late. I think we should go.

959
01:05:09,864 --> 01:05:12,084
I'm glad she's okay.

960
01:05:12,477 --> 01:05:14,569
- Goodbye.
- Wait!

961
01:05:14,571 --> 01:05:15,962
What time do you finish work?

962
01:05:15,964 --> 01:05:18,124
I'd like to wait and treat you to a meal.

963
01:05:18,804 --> 01:05:21,331
No thanks. Consider it eaten. Take care.

964
01:05:21,333 --> 01:05:26,002
No, my mom insisted I treat you
and bring back the receipt.

965
01:05:26,150 --> 01:05:27,624
I'll wait!

966
01:05:28,200 --> 01:05:29,280
What?

967
01:05:31,611 --> 01:05:32,955
We have a company dinner.

968
01:05:32,957 --> 01:05:35,110
Don't wait, just leave.

969
01:05:37,284 --> 01:05:38,410
A company dinner?

970
01:05:39,838 --> 01:05:41,204
I have to treat her today.

971
01:05:59,311 --> 01:06:01,704
Are you that kind to everyone?

972
01:06:02,151 --> 01:06:03,224
Excuse me?

973
01:06:12,131 --> 01:06:14,194
If you're that kind and thoughtful
to everyone,

974
01:06:14,196 --> 01:06:16,197
what do you do
for the person you really like?

975
01:06:17,311 --> 01:06:19,644
I'm not sure what you mean.

976
01:06:19,797 --> 01:06:22,625
You're not dating everyone.

977
01:06:22,653 --> 01:06:24,704
You should make it clear,

978
01:06:24,737 --> 01:06:26,604
so the person you like
doesn't get jealous.

979
01:06:26,671 --> 01:06:30,237
Then spell it out for me.

980
01:06:35,217 --> 01:06:37,004
Can't you save that kindness just for me?

981
01:06:37,764 --> 01:06:38,764
What?

982
01:06:42,490 --> 01:06:45,759
I know you're just being nice.
Helping that old lady,

983
01:06:46,034 --> 01:06:47,399
and all, that's great,

984
01:06:47,580 --> 01:06:50,111
but giving your lunch
to someone just because he looks hungry,

985
01:06:50,592 --> 01:06:52,091
smiling at him for no reason,

986
01:06:52,652 --> 01:06:55,435
answering all his nonsense.
Can't you just stop doing that?

987
01:06:55,436 --> 01:06:57,705
The man you're nice to and take care of,

988
01:06:57,827 --> 01:06:59,311
can't it just be me?

989
01:07:00,444 --> 01:07:02,611
I don't understand...

990
01:07:03,004 --> 01:07:05,510
You really don't get it, do you?

991
01:07:08,204 --> 01:07:09,307
Right now,

992
01:07:10,494 --> 01:07:12,024
I'm confessing.

993
01:07:12,397 --> 01:07:13,421
Just...

994
01:07:13,949 --> 01:07:15,611
look at me.

995
01:07:18,751 --> 01:07:20,968
I think I've fallen for you. Gyu Rim.

996
01:07:22,016 --> 01:07:23,090
Now do you get it?

997
01:08:02,630 --> 01:08:05,963
(Love on the Menu)

998
01:08:06,211 --> 01:08:08,282
- There's a woman I like.
- Mu Jin.

999
01:08:08,284 --> 01:08:10,777
If you just support me, Mom,
I won't give her up.

1000
01:08:10,780 --> 01:08:13,790
Honestly, what her parents do,
what her job is,

1001
01:08:13,791 --> 01:08:15,459
what her siblings do,

1002
01:08:15,461 --> 01:08:18,162
isn't it normal for the chairwoman
to check all that?

1003
01:08:18,164 --> 01:08:20,619
- Why do I live like this?
- You're the firstborn.

1004
01:08:20,621 --> 01:08:21,929
Because you're kind.

1005
01:08:21,931 --> 01:08:25,129
Always yielding, selfless,
a compassionate firstborn.

1006
01:08:25,130 --> 01:08:26,241
I'm getting married.

1007
01:08:26,243 --> 01:08:29,011
Han Gyu Yeong,
what if I start living like you?

1008
01:08:29,013 --> 01:08:31,810
Is that part-timer really dating Mu Jin?

1009
01:08:31,857 --> 01:08:36,250
I'm telling you,
I also have feelings for you.

1010
01:08:36,440 --> 01:08:38,240
Dramaday.me
